								<span id="lblHtml"><font size="2"><P><SPAN class=title>Points and looting rights</SPAN> </P>
<P>
<HR SIZE=1>

<P></P>
<P>We&nbsp;have to move over to a point system. Deveau, Aquaella,&nbsp;and I will be working on the webmaintance of it. The guild is getting larger and we feel pretty much as a whole that not only is the current method being outgrown. Also we feel that that people should be able to get loot more evenly distributed.&nbsp;&nbsp;The pp on the raid will go to guild bank for large investments in coffins and stones :). This is only pp collection is on official raids.&nbsp;These are&nbsp;currently Wednesday and Sundays/Saturday Official raids. I try to plan the more important raids on these days and they are fully funded by the guild, as opposed to unofficial raids (like fridays) in which we farm and get together for just what ever reason ;).<BR><BR>If there is a dispute on attendance contact Akashau. Aquaella, Deveau and&nbsp;myself will be doing attendance. This is a check and balance system. This auction is to be done silently. Do not say oh I am bidding on that, just send the bid when its called, don`t clutter the screen with garble <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src="http://www.ezboard.com/images/emoticons/smile.gif"><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> <BR><BR>Points will be award to which ever character is present, they will not be poolable. The reason for this is the program doesn`t connect the alts, and it does create a link for each listed character. It also makes more work for the person running bidding and board updater.<BR><BR><!--EZCODE AUTOLINK START--><A href="/">hallsofhaven.guildwizard.com/</A><!--EZCODE AUTOLINK END--> check it out under roster click your name, and sign in <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src="http://www.ezboard.com/images/emoticons/smile.gif"><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> <BR><BR>You must have enough points. NO EXCEPTIONS. No Negative points, no credit. Please know your points<BR><BR>If your the only class that needs an item/no drop and its an upgrade then the point system will not apply it will be defaulted to you. No reason to let it rot.<BR><BR>Attendance - Attendance is taken every hour. 1 point is awarded for coming on time. Attendace will be taken pretty much at unknown time and when everyone is in zone. Three hour raid is 3 points for full attendance, and 4 total points for being on time as well. People arriving late will recieve less points.<BR><BR>Bidding - Droppable and No Drop loot will be NBG bidded on first silently. This means a tell is sent to the designated Bid Collector with the amount you wish to bid. If you are the highest it will be announced by Collector, and you will be allowed to loot or be given the item. Items not claimed by NBG will be silent auctioned and given out during the raid&nbsp; if they are no drop. Example, golden efreeti boots drop, no one needs them as upgrade, everyone is called to send the silent auction after raid, winner is called out. Example, golden efreeti boots drop, 2 people claim them as upgrade, they each send the silent auction, winner is called out.</P>
<P>Points to establish looting order - Example a rareish item such as a lucid shard drops in ME on a raid, this will be give to the person needing the shard with the most points earned (not able to be spent). This will establish a looting order allowing those that play the most to get keys and key pieces first for guild utilization. <!--EZCODE ITALIC START--><!--EZCODE ITALIC END--><BR><BR>Ties - in the event of a tie on silent bid, the member with the most points will be awarded the item for the points bidded. Example, I bid 10 and you bid 10, and I have 97 points and you have 107, you will win the item and deduct 10 points. These points are the points that you have to spend, not that you have earned in the past.</P>
<P>Caps - We will currently cap items at 20 points. This means no items will cost over 20 points. In the event of a tie the person with the most raid points will win the bid. If its still tied then those two will roll.<BR><BR>You pay what you bid.<BR><BR>We will not have minimum points for BP and other items. A silent bid will be called on desired items and tells sent to the designated bid counter.<BR><BR>Droppable loot - At first, only classes that can use can participate in the silent auction at the end of the raid. If no bids are made on the item anyone else can bid regardless of class. If no one bids at that point its randomed for zero cost to players.<BR><BR>Also, a one time 3 points will be given in the beginning of this for each person who has magelo registration, a custom signature (the custom signature should link back to your gear), and guildmagic registration. This will start you off with 3 points total. Like a free raid <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src="http://www.ezboard.com/images/emoticons/smile.gif"><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> There might be some reading involved. We are here to help you with this.<BR><BR>This will be ammended as issues arise. I have never run a point system.</P>
<P><BR><!--EZCODE LINK START--><A href="http://spinpcycle.serverpro2.com/guestpoints.htm" target=top>Guest points</A><!--EZCODE LINK END--><BR>AoP and regular raiders that come to HoH hosted events will earn loot points like regular members.</P>
